#, php-format
msgid "A full list of the tools and health checks in version %s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: PublishRank version number.
#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:127
#, php-format
msgid "This inventory for version %s covers every dashboard tool card and Technical Health check. Search & discovery includes Schema studio, Sitemap health, IndexNow, Search Console, Search engines, Google Preferred Sources, Robots.txt, Crawl optimization, Breadcrumbs, Site verification, AI & llms.txt and Schema Aggregator. Content & publishing includes SEO score, SEO Overrides, Google Discover image, Author expertise, Local SEO, Image optimizer, Publisher toolkit, Newsroom, Planning board, Newsroom calendar, Newsroom activity, My notifications, Newsroom configuration, Newsroom roles, Content Graph and Link Health Audit. Measure & maintain includes Publisher analytics, Insights, Redirects, 404 monitor, Traffic Guard, WP Private Login, Configuration history and Diagnostics. Settings & help includes Setup wizard, Features, Settings, Titles & Meta, Import / Export and Help & documentation. Technical Health checks include SEO plugin conflicts, Search engine visibility, Pretty permalinks, HTTPS, News sitemap, Structured data coverage, Publisher logo, Default social image, Robots.txt and JNews compatibility. Some features are optional or permission-gated and external integrations require their own configuration; this list describes what the package provides, not a guarantee that every optional service is active on every site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:129
msgid "Browse all tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:134
msgid "Finding your way around"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:135
msgid "Every PublishRank screen shares the same side menu, grouped by task."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:136
msgid "Every PublishRank screen has the same layout: the page header on top, a side menu on the left and the tool itself on the right. The side menu lists Dashboard, Features, General Settings and Sitemap Hub first, followed by groups for Search & discovery, Content & publishing, Newsroom, Measure & maintain and Help. Select a group name to open or close it; the group of the screen you are on opens automatically. The WordPress sidebar keeps a short list of essentials, and the toolbar entry offers shortcuts to the Dashboard, Newsroom, Titles & Meta, Settings, Setup Wizard and this help screen. The PublishRank mark is the only logo the plugin uses."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:141
msgid "Titles, descriptions & canonical URLs"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:142
msgid "How the search title and snippet are chosen, and when to set your own."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:143
msgid "PublishRank generates title and description fallbacks from WordPress content and templates. A custom title or description should be used when an editor needs a specific search snippet. Canonical URLs identify the preferred public URL; do not point them at unrelated pages."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:150
msgid "Title & description variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:151
msgid "Placeholders such as %%title%% and %%sitename%% that fill in automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:152
#, php-format
msgid "Dynamic variables work in per-post SEO titles, meta descriptions, social titles, social descriptions and the homepage title and description. Use the “Insert variable” list under each field; it shows every supported variable grouped by Site, Content, Author, Taxonomy, Dates and SEO, with what each returns and what happens when it is empty. Typed tokens look like %%title%% and %%sitename%%; %%sep%% is your configured title separator, %%page%% adds “Page 2” on later pages and %%permalink%% is the canonical URL. The older %focus_keyword% form also works. Variables are replaced once, unknown variables are dropped, and a separator left dangling by an empty value is removed. Results are plain text; they are escaped when printed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:157
msgid "Output controls & what PublishRank can override"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:158
msgid "Which parts of the page PublishRank controls, and which belong to your theme."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:159
msgid "Settings > Output controls and Breadcrumbs switch PublishRank metadata, the JSON-LD graph, the Organization/WebSite entities, the visible breadcrumb trail and BreadcrumbList data on or off independently; all are on for new installs and your saved choices are kept on upgrade. Changes to your publication identity apply to every page automatically. PublishRank controls only its own head metadata, JSON-LD and breadcrumb trail: a logo, site title, breadcrumb trail or meta tags that your theme or another plugin hard-codes belong to that theme or plugin. If your theme prints its own breadcrumbs choose \"Structured data only\"; if it prints a second title or description, disable that in the theme. Pages cached by a caching plugin or CDN need a purge after a change (PublishRank fires the publishrank_seo_output_settings_changed action for cache plugins)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:161
msgid "Open General Settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:166
msgid "Schema & publisher identity"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:167
msgid "Structured data that tells search engines who publishes each story."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:168
msgid "Organization, NewsArticle, author, breadcrumb and media structured data help describe the publication and its content. Complete the publisher identity and logo fields accurately. Do not add custom JSON-LD that duplicates or contradicts generated entities."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:170
msgid "Open Schema"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:175
msgid "Breadcrumb separators"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:176
msgid "Pick the character shown between breadcrumb links."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:177
msgid "Pick a preset (arrows, angles, slashes and lines, dots, dashes, symbols, spaced variants, a space, a non-breaking space, or none) or type your own up to 10 characters. The separator is plain text, so HTML is not allowed; leading and trailing spaces are kept. It is visual only and never appears in BreadcrumbList structured data."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:179
msgid "Open Breadcrumbs"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:184
msgid "XML, News, image & video sitemaps"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:185
msgid "The files that help search engines find every story you publish."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:186
msgid "The sitemap index links to the enabled sitemap types. News sitemaps focus on eligible recent articles; image and video sitemaps help describe media attached to eligible content. Check Sitemap Hub after changing permalink, sitemap or cache settings. A sitemap is a discovery hint, not an indexing guarantee."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:188
#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:357
#: src/Admin/SEOScorePage.php:76
#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1257
msgid "Open Sitemap Hub"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:193
msgid "Reading your sitemap in a browser"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:194
msgid "What the friendly sitemap page shows and how to read it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:195
msgid "Open your sitemap index in a browser to see a readable overview. The top explains what the file is and gives you the one address to submit, with copy and Search Console shortcuts. Below it, a short three-step strip explains how sitemaps work, four totals show how many addresses, content types and files are listed and when the newest change happened, and the “What’s in your sitemap” list shows one row per content type with its icon, a plain description, the number of addresses, its share of the total and when it last changed. An empty row is normal: it fills up automatically when matching content is published. Open a row to see every address in that file, with filtering, paging and quick checks (URL limit, last-modified dates, HTTPS and news data). Search engines never use this view; they read the plain XML. Use View raw XML to see exactly what crawlers receive. Very large indexes skip per-file URL counts to stay fast."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:197
msgid "Open your sitemap"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:203
msgid "Robots, archives & indexing controls"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:204
msgid "Decide what search engines may crawl and index."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:205
msgid "Robots settings influence crawling and indexing signals. Use noindex carefully, especially on article pages and category archives. robots.txt rules are not a substitute for access control and do not guarantee removal from search results."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:207
msgid "Open Robots.txt"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:213
msgid "Tell Bing and other IndexNow engines as soon as a story changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:214
msgid "IndexNow can notify supported participating search engines about URL changes after you enable it and configure its verification key. Notifications do not guarantee indexing, and Google does not use IndexNow."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:216
msgid "Open IndexNow"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:221
msgid "Baidu URL submission"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:222
msgid "Send new addresses to Baidu from a verified site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:223
msgid "Baidu requires a verified site and its current site-specific ordinary-inclusion endpoint. PublishRank stores that HTTPS endpoint encrypted, limits requests to the same host and batches up to 2,000 URLs. Baidu quota and eligibility vary; acceptance is not an indexing guarantee. Baidu dashboard analytics are not exposed through a documented public read API."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:225
msgid "Open Search engines"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:230
msgid "Google Search Console & local analytics"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:231
msgid "Connect Search Console and read your publishing trends."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:232
msgid "The optional Search Console connection uses Google OAuth webmasters.readonly, requires a Google Cloud project with the Search Console API enabled, and stores tokens encrypted at rest. Refreshes are administrator-initiated; data is aggregated and delayed. Local Publisher Analytics is separate and does not track visitors. Never paste OAuth client secrets or tokens into public support requests."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:239
msgid "Editorial SEO intelligence"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:240
msgid "The live score and checks that help editors before publishing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:241
msgid "Article analysis reviews signals such as headline, keyphrase, description, structure, readability, media and links. Treat scores and suggestions as editorial guidance, not a promise of ranking performance. Always prioritize accuracy and reader value."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:248
msgid "Live blogs, Newsroom & news workflow"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:249
msgid "Live coverage markup and the built-in editorial workflow."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:250
msgid "Choose Live Blog Post in the Schema box and add timestamped updates to mark a live blog; ordinary posts are never marked up as live blogs automatically. The built-in Newsroom handles story pitches, assignments, workflow stages, a planning board, a calendar and private notes. These are editorial aids and do not change what is published until you publish."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:257
msgid "Images, media & performance"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:258
msgid "Keep images sharp, light and ready for Google Discover."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:259
msgid "Image optimization settings control supported image-processing behavior. Keep originals or backups according to your workflow, test output with your theme and CDN, and verify that image dimensions and quality remain suitable for publishing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:261
msgid "Open Image optimizer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:266
msgid "Redirects & 404 monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:267
msgid "Fix broken links and send old addresses to the right page."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:268
msgid "Use permanent redirects for durable URL moves and temporary redirects when the move is temporary. Test the destination and avoid redirect loops/chains. The 404 Monitor is opt-in and records normalized GET/HEAD 404 paths only; admin, AJAX, cron, REST, non-HTML asset and common infrastructure-probe requests are excluded. Hits are aggregated by browser, mobile or crawler category without IP addresses, cookies, request bodies or full query strings. Administrators can search, filter, sort, dismiss, clear and create validated same-site redirects from the monitor. Its 90-day, 500-entry rolling limit, rate limiting and write lock make it a bounded diagnostic aid rather than a complete access log, analytics system or WAF."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:270
msgid "Open Redirects"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:275
msgid "Diagnostics & compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:276
msgid "Check plugin health and spot clashes with other SEO plugins."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:277
msgid "Run diagnostics after installation or major configuration changes. Review conflicts with themes and other SEO plugins, then inspect the live page source and sitemap responses. Disable overlapping SEO output in other plugins only after confirming which plugin owns each output."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:284
msgid "Settings import/export & configuration history"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:285
msgid "Back up your settings and see what changed and when."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:286
msgid "Use exports for controlled migration and backups. Review imported settings before relying on them, and protect exported files. Configuration history can help identify changes; it is not a substitute for a full database backup."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:288
msgid "Open Import / Export"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:293
msgid "Versions, updates & support"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:294
msgid "Where the version number appears and what to do after updating."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:295
msgid "The plugin version appears on every PublishRank screen header, in the sitemap view footer, in the plugin header and in the readme stable tag; all of them always show the same number. After updating, clear your site, plugin, CDN and browser caches so you see the current admin styles and sitemap stylesheet. If something looks wrong, run Diagnostics and Sitemap Hub first, then check for conflicts with other SEO plugins."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:305
msgid "My sitemap shows a blank page or plain text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:306
msgid "Open Settings › Permalinks in WordPress and select Save Changes without changing anything. This refreshes the address rules. Then reload your sitemap."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:309
msgid "The sitemap page looks unstyled"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:310
msgid "Purge your page, CDN and browser caches, then reload. The sitemap design is generated by WordPress at /publishrank-sitemap.xsl, so a caching layer that rewrites or blocks that address can break it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:313
msgid "The Google News sitemap is empty"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:314
msgid "That is normal when nothing was published recently. It only lists eligible articles from the news window (48 hours by default), and an empty sitemap is still valid."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:317
msgid "I see duplicate titles or schema in my page source"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:318
msgid "Two plugins (or your theme and a plugin) are printing the same thing. Leave only one of them responsible for each output, then purge caches."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:321
msgid "I changed a setting but my site still shows the old version"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:322
msgid "Clear your site, plugin, CDN and browser caches. Cached pages keep showing the previous output until they are refreshed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:325
msgid "The PublishRank icon is missing from the menu or toolbar"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:326
msgid "Purge caches and confirm that assets/images/publishrank-brand-mark.png exists inside the plugin folder and is readable."
msgstr ""

